CATEGORIES:Guided Walk,MAP,CBD
DTSTAMP:20261006T120213Z
DESCRIPTION:Join Aayati Sengupta\, Curator of Grip\, Hold\, Pin\, for a walkthrough of the exhibition. Through a close reading of the works on view\, the walkthrough will explore wrestling as more than a sport—as a site where discipline\, kinship\, identity and everyday life converge. Drawing on photography\, archival material and moving image\, Grip\, Hold\, Pin traces the histories and lived experiences that shape wrestling cultures across India\, inviting audiences to consider the relationships between body\, labour\, tradition and representation.
DTEND:20261011T063000Z
DTSTART:20261011T053000Z
SUMMARY:Grip\, Hold\, Pin - Curator walkthrough
UID:1415@map-india.org
URL:https://map-india.org/map-events/grip-hold-pin-curator-walkthrough/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://map-india.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/MAP-Website-7.jpg
CATEGORIES:Guided Walk,MAP,CBD
DTSTAMP:20261006T121703Z
DESCRIPTION:Experience Grip\, Hold\, Pin: Wrestling in India through a Deaf-led walkthrough that invites audiences to look closely at how wrestling\, wrestlers and the world of kushti have been represented through photography.\n\nLed by Akanksha Kamble from the MAP team\, this visual-first walkthrough explores the exhibition’s photographs documenting the lives\, identities and expressions of wrestlers across India. The walkthrough opens up conversations around the physicality of wrestling\, the spaces in which it is practised\, and the people and communities that shape its traditions.
DTEND:20261010T103000Z
DTSTART:20261010T093000Z
SUMMARY:Grip\, Hold\, Pin - Deaf Led walkthrough
UID:1417@map-india.org
URL:https://map-india.org/map-events/grip-hold-pin-deaf-led-walkthrough/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://map-india.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/MAP-Website-4.jpg
CATEGORIES:Film Screenings,MAP,CBD
DTSTAMP:20261006T090254Z
DESCRIPTION:Goonga Pehelwan follows the extraordinary journey of Virender Singh\, one of India’s most accomplished deaf wrestlers\, as he pursues his dream of representing India at the 2016 Rio Olympics.\nBorn and raised in a small village in Haryana\, Virender began wrestling at a young age and went on to build an exceptional career\, including multiple Deaflympics and World Deaf Wrestling Championship medals. Yet\, despite his achievements on the mat\, he faced persistent barriers and limited recognition from India’s sporting establishment.\n\nMoving between the wrestling arena\, his village and the institutions that determine the fate of athletes like him\, the film explores the battles Virender faces both inside and outside the ring. Goonga Pehelwan is a portrait of an athlete whose determination to compete at the highest level becomes a larger story about recognition\, access and the struggles faced by deaf athletes in India.\n\nJoin the filmmaker\, Vivek Chaudhary and Virender Singh for a conversation following the screening\, as they reflect on the film and the story behind it.
DTEND:20261010T120000Z
DTSTART:20261010T103000Z
SUMMARY:Goonga Pehelwan
UID:1414@map-india.org
URL:https://map-india.org/map-events/goonga-pehelwan-2/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://map-india.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/MAP-Website-2.jpg
CATEGORIES:Drop-in Sessions,MAP,CBD
DTSTAMP:20261005T140246Z
DESCRIPTION:Ever wondered how wrestling was depicted before photography—and what these early images can tell us about the way we have understood sport\, strength and the body?\n\nJoin Shubhashree from MAP’s Education Department as she explores depictions of women wrestling in the Raagmala paintings featured in Grip\, Hold\, Pin. Looking closely at these early works\, the walkthrough will consider how wrestling has long existed beyond the mat—as part of India’s visual and cultural traditions—and how ideas of gender\, strength\, movement and identity have been represented through art across time.
DTEND:20261009T120000Z
DTSTART:20261009T113000Z
SUMMARY:Up\, Close and Centre
UID:1411@map-india.org
URL:https://map-india.org/map-events/up-close-and-centre-5/
